WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.490
Samsung’s Galaxy S10 is gonna be announced
at their Unpacked event on February 20th,

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:08.170
and there’s recently been a ton of leaks
surrounding specs and final design.

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:13.299
We’re expecting 3 different models, including
the S10+, which is said to be packing some

00:00:13.299 --> 00:00:14.950
impressive performance specs.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:19.180
The question for a lot of us is if the iPhone
XS is still gonna hold the crown for the fastest

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:20.610
smartphone available.

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:23.940
Hit that Like button and we’ll go through
all of the recent S10 leaks and see what we

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.130
should expect on February 20th.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:31.950
Last year, in April, 91Mobiles leaked renders
of the Galaxy S10+, featuring a bezel-less

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:35.769
design with a hole-punch dual-lens selfie
camera on the front of the phone.

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:40.719
Earlier this year, we also saw images of the
regular S10 model, with a single-lens hole-punch

00:00:40.719 --> 00:00:44.949
instead, and we’ve seen multiple leaked
images that basically confirm what the front

00:00:44.949 --> 00:00:45.949
will look like.

00:00:45.949 --> 00:00:50.219
There was also a rumor of the S10 featuring
reverse wireless charging, which was almost

00:00:50.219 --> 00:00:55.559
confirmed by a leaked legit-looking render
of the Samsung’s upcoming Galaxy Buds sitting

00:00:55.559 --> 00:00:56.890
on top of the S10.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:01.899
The Galaxy Buds are meant to be a direct rival
to Apple’s AirPods, and yes, we will definitely

00:01:01.899 --> 00:01:05.960
be doing a comparison between the two, so
subscribe now so you don’t miss that!

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:10.290
The S10+ is said to feature a dual-lens camera
in the front and a triple-lens camera in the

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:13.780
back, as seen by these seemingly official
leaked renders.

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:17.760
The cheaper S10 model would keep the triple
lens rear camera but switch to a single lens

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:18.940
in the front.

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:22.670
Both of those models are said to support a
fingerprint sensor under the display.

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:27.880
The even cheaper S10e, may not support in-display
fingerprint sensing tech, and will simply

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:31.190
have a dual-lens camera on the back, just
like the Note 9.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.670
Now let’s talk performance.

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:38.100
Geekbench 4 benchmark scores from the Galaxy
S10+’s Snapdragon 855 processor have been

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:45.140
leaked, featuring a 3413 single-core and 10256
multi-core scores.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:52.740
The Exynox 9820-powered model was also leaked,
with scores of 4382 single-core and 9570 multi-core.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:58.600
Interestingly, those scores put the S10+ on-par
with the iPhone X from 2017.

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:04.500
The iPhone XS, XS Max, and XR completely blow
both processors out of the water, with a single-core

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:10.090
score of 4795 and a single-core score of 11,267.

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:14.040
So from those leaks, the latest iPhones really
don’t have anything to worry about, since

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:18.920
Samsung’s 2019 smartphone will most likely
pack these underpowered processors.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:23.969
On top of that, iPhones are usually better
optimized for performance and RAM management.

00:02:23.969 --> 00:02:29.829
Also leaked was some Antutu benchmark scores,
with the S10+ scoring 325,000 points, still

00:02:29.829 --> 00:02:35.000
less than the iPhone XS’ record-holding
352,000 points, so the iPhone doesn’t seem

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.510
to have anything to worry about in terms of
graphics either.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:41.430
Apple has been doing a great job of increasing
processor performance every year for the last

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:45.750
few years, so we’re expecting future iPhones
to hold the performance crown as well.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:51.409
Back to Samsung S10 leaks, Evan Blass posted
a seemingly official image of the Galaxy S10

00:02:51.409 --> 00:02:56.209
lineup, looking similar to a Galaxy Note 9,
except with a long and narrow camera bump

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:58.599
and the removal of the fingerprint sensor.

00:02:58.599 --> 00:03:03.049
FCC filings also showed that the Galaxy S10
could be one of the first devices to support

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:07.219
WiFi 6, which has also been rumored for the
2019 iPhones.

00:03:07.219 --> 00:03:11.830
So with all of those leaks, there’s no doubt
the Galaxy S10 will be a great lineup of phones,

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:15.239
packing some new tech we’re hoping to see
in future iPhones as well.

00:03:15.239 --> 00:03:19.390
As far as performance, we still expect the
iPhone XS to outperform the new S10 devices,

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:24.280
and we’ll be comparing everything from performance
to camera quality as soon as they get released,

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:25.540
so make sure to subscribe for that!

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:28.239
What are your thoughts on the upcoming Galaxy
S10?

00:03:28.239 --> 00:03:29.739
Let us know in the comment section below!

00:03:29.739 --> 00:03:31.909
Thanks for watching, and we’ll see you in
the next one.

